        "department": null,
        "description": "Recent years have seen a surge in the applications of multi-robot systems. This course will focus on decision making of the robots in different settings -- centralized, decentralized, non-cooperative, deterministic and probabilistic. Game theoretic and algorithmic techniques for robot planning and coordination will be covered. This course will emphasize on theoretical aspects as well as hands-on using platforms such as ROS (Robot Operating Systems), Gazebo/Webots, Python/C++ implementations in the applications of multi-robot surveillance, smart mobility (EVs, ride-sharing), warehouse robots etc. Course project will focus on multi-robot planning/ scheduling/ task allocation in deterministic/ stochastic settings.",
